{"type":"message","id":"b6fd122b","parentId":"5ee542b4","timestamp":"2026-05-21T03:46:03.320Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the results:\n\n**Arbitration thread**: Latest messages are heartbeat messages from 23:50 UTC (timestamps around 1778975520833). The last few are just \"[Heartbeat 23:50 UTC]\" - very brief versions.\n\n**General thread**: Latest messages are heartbeat messages from 23:45 UTC (timestamps around 1778975171537).\n\nBoth threads show automated heartbeat messages only - no human discussions requiring responses.\n\nThe timestamps I see:\n- Latest arbitration: 1778975520833 (23:50 UTC) - two brief heartbeats\n- Latest general: 1778975171537 (23:45 UTC)\n\nCurrent time is 03:45 AM UTC on May 21, 2026. Let me convert the timestamps to see where we are.\n\n1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds from epoch\nLet me calculate... the latest message timestamps are from around 23:50 UTC on what appears to be May 20, 2026.\n\nWait, let me check more carefully. The timestamps:\n- 1778975520833 / 1000 = 1778975520.833 seconds\n- 1778974608000 would be 23:45 UTC on May 20, 2026\n- Current time is 03:45 UTC on May 21, 2026\n\nLet me estimate the gap:\nFrom 23:50 to 03:45 = about 4 hours 55 minutes = 295 minutes = 17700000 ms\n\nSo the latest messages were 1778975520833, and current time in ms would be approximately 1778975520833 + (4 hours worth) = 1778975520833 + 14400000 ≈ 1778989920833\n\nBut that's not right because my calculation shows the current time should be around May 21 03:45. Let me just calculate:\n\n\n23:45 UTC May 20 to 03:45 UTC May 21 = 4 hours = 14400000 ms\n1778975171537 + 14400000 = 1778989571537 ms\n\nSo current time is approximately 1778989571537 ms.\n\nThe latest arbitration message at 1778975520833 is about 14 million milliseconds or ~3.9 hours behind. The latest general message at 1778975171537 is about 4 hours 2 minutes behind. So there are no new messages from humans - all messages